/P 269 0 R
/E (Response: The Society previously maintained offices in Kitwe and Livingstone but closed them due to high operational costs relative to collections. The establishment of provincial branches is contingent on increased revenue, which in turn depends on the amendment of the Copyright Act. ZAMCOPS acknowledged that many provincial radio stations remain non-compliant and reiterated that the IBA partnership is intended to address this.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [11]
>>
